From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add a driver for the Samsung OIS MCU

The Galaxy Z Flip3's rear wide camera stabilises its lens with an
STM32G0 running Samsung's firmware (stock cam_ois_mcu_stm32g.c). Drive
it as stock does, without any help from userspace:

- It powers up and down with its camera sensor: a runtime PM device
  link with the sensor (samsung,camera-sensor) as consumer, so it is on
  while the sensor streams, for any V4L2 or libcamera user.
- Power-up is the camera HAL's sequence (vdig, vaf, vio, 5 ms, NRST,
  BOOT0 low), then stock's cam_ois_init(): wait for status 0x01 or
  0x13, the module EEPROM's gyro gains if their mark is 0xbb, gyro
  polarity, orientation and zero offsets, centre shift compensation
  from focus position 0x80, gyro gain fade times of 1000, the compensation
  angle, and the HAL's init setting (OISSEL = module 1). Then the lens
  is centred for 40 ms, and the servo runs in the selected mode.
- Modes are the HAL's: still (0x00, its default), movie (0x01) and
  centering (0x05, what it uses with stabilisation off), chosen in
  sysfs.
- The focus position (the lens's V4L2_CID_FOCUS_ABSOLUTE >> 4, as stock's
  actuator driver passes it) goes to CAAFPOSM1 on every change, through
  a control notifier on the sensor's lens-focus.
- The gyro zero offsets come from stock's factory calibration, which
  the HAL reads from /efs/FactoryApp/camera_ois_gyro_cal (comma-separated
  degrees per second with three decimals; it drops the dots and takes
  the first three fields as x, y and z) and the kernel scales by
  114/1000 at power-up. The same text goes into the gyro_calibration
  attribute and applies at the next power-up. Like stock, Z is written
  as 0.
- Like stock, a failed start is logged and the sensor still streams,
  and power-down turns no servo off.

The probe powers the MCU once and logs its firmware version. The status
attribute shows the status and error registers and, with the servo on,
the gyro targets and hall positions as stock's
cam_ois_read_hall_position() reads them. System sleep powers it down
through runtime PM.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---

diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-i2c-devices-samsung-ois-mcu b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-i2c-devices-samsung-ois-mcu
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7123341
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-bus-i2c-devices-samsung-ois-mcu
@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../mode
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.3
+Contact:	Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+Description:
+		(RW) The mode the lens is stabilised in while the camera
+		sensor is powered: "still" (the default, Samsung's camera
+		for photos), "movie" (for video) or "centering" (the lens
+		held centred, no stabilisation). A change applies at once
+		when the MCU is on.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../gyro_calibration
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.3
+Contact:	Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+Description:
+		(RW) The gyro zero offsets of this phone, in the format of
+		Samsung's /efs/FactoryApp/camera_ois_gyro_cal as Samsung's
+		camera HAL reads it: "x,y" or "x,y,z", each in degrees per
+		second with three decimals, as Samsung's factory calibration
+		measures them. X and Y are written to the MCU at its next
+		power-up, Z is kept but not used (Samsung's driver writes 0).
+		Defaults to 0.000,0.000,0.000.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../status
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.3
+Contact:	Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+Description:
+		(RO) "off" while the MCU is powered down; while it is on, its
+		status and error registers, whether the servo is on, the mode
+		register, the 8-bit focus position last passed to it (-1 if
+		none yet) and the lens hall centre it reported. With the
+		servo on, also the X and Y gyro targets and hall positions,
+		read once (this takes about 105 ms).
+
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/.../firmware_version
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.3
+Contact:	Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
+Description:
+		(RO) The MCU firmware version read at probe, in Samsung's
+		8-character form (core version, driver IC, MCU, gyro, year,
+		month, release count, development or release mark).
